  "claim_short": "If a compactly supported finite measure on a graded group satisfies the Govindan Sheri--Hickman--Wright curvature assumption, subtracting a compactly supported smooth function with the same mass produces a mean-zero measure which satisfies the positive- and negative-order Rockland Fourier conditions, for the measure and its reflection. The reverse implication is not proved.",
